<!--
  HuntableHerds data. Read by HerdBuildData.BuildAll() from the folder the assembly lives in
  (Modules/RealmsForgotten/bin/Win64_Shipping_Client), so this file must be copied next to
  HuntableHerds.dll.

  Per-herd tuning:
    notifMessage / messageTitle / message  REPEATABLE. One is picked at random per notification,
                                           which is what keeps the map notices from reading the same
                                           four lines forever.
    spawnId          ItemObject id of the animal (its <Horse monster="..."> decides the action set).
    totalAmountInHerd  Animals spawned over the hunt. Hard-clamped by
                       Settings.MaxAliveAnimalsPerHunt, so huge values here are safe but pointless.
    isPassive        true  -> PassiveHerdAgentComponent: only flees.
                     false -> AggressiveHerdAgentComponent: chase / telegraph / bite / short recoil.
    sightRange       METERS. It is now really used as a distance (it used to be passed into the
                     view-cone angle slot, which made the cone always true and pinned the real
                     distance at the 30m default).
    hitboxRange      METERS at which a blow can land. The wind-up starts
                     Settings.TelegraphExtraRange meters earlier.
    fleeOnAttacked   MUST match isPassive. An aggressive animal with fleeOnAttacked=true was the
                     old "bite and run away" bug: every hit cancelled its pursuit.
                     Want deer / sheep to be fleeing prey instead of fighters? Set BOTH
                     isPassive=true and fleeOnAttacked=true on that entry.
    terrain          OPTIONAL, repeatable. Campaign-map TerrainType names (Plain, Forest, Steppe,
                     Desert, Snow, Mountain, Swamp, Dune, RuralArea, Canyon, Beach, ...). When
                     present, the herd is only offered while the main party stands on one of them.
                     No <terrain> entries = any terrain. Can be switched off globally with
                     Settings.FilterHerdsByTerrain.
-->
